    {
      "term": "B-Group",
      "matchText": "B-Group",
      "definition": "A short-lived archaeological label that early excavators briefly applied to a layer of Lower Nubian graves between the A-Group and C-Group. Re-examination showed the \"B-Group\" graves were just poorer A-Group burials in different clothing, not a distinct culture, and the label was officially retired. There is no B-Group; the letter is a placeholder for a gap.",
      "type": "concept"
    },
