      "term": "Upper Nubia",
      "matchText": "Upper Nubia",
      "wikiSlug": "",
      "type": "place",
      "definition": "Upper Nubia is the southern stretch of the ancient Nubian Nile, roughly between the Second and Sixth Cataracts in what is now northern Sudan — Kerma country. (\"Upper\" here means upstream/southern, the same convention as Upper Egypt.) The Egyptians considered it the deeper, more dangerous Nubia: harder to reach, harder to control, and the heart of any kingdom strong enough to make Egyptian pharaohs nervous."
